## Error Handling

- Return `error` as last return value; wrap with `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)`
- Use sentinel errors (`var ErrNotFound = errors.New(...)`) for expected conditions callers need to match
- Log at the boundary where the error is handled, not at every intermediate layer

## Naming

- Packages: short, lowercase, singular (`provider`, `routing`, `config`)
- Interfaces: behavior-based names, not `I`-prefixed (`HealthTracker`, `SPForwarder`, `Publisher`)
- Constructors: `New<Type>(deps...) *Type` — panic on nil required deps, document nil-safe optional deps

## Dependencies

- Constructor injection, no globals or init()
- Required deps panic on nil in constructor; optional deps are nil-checked at use site
- Interfaces defined where consumed, not where implemented

## Struct Layout

```go
type Router struct {
	// required deps (injected, never nil after construction)
	registry      *provider.Registry
	healthTracker provider.HealthTracker
	// optional deps (nil-checked at use site)
	forwarder     SPForwarder
	// config
	config        config.RoutingConfig
	// infra
	logger        *slog.Logger
}
```

## Logging

Use `log/slog` structured logging. Include contextual key-value pairs. Correlation
fields use a single canonical snake_case name each — `resource_id`, `ce_id`,
`ce_type`, `service_type`, `provider_id` — never camelCase variants:
```go
r.logger.Info("dispatching operation", "resource_id", resourceID, "service_type", serviceType)
```
